diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 64a09fe..3bb1222 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -29,6 +29,30 @@ Usage
     $ READ_FUSES out_file -> Dumps the T124 fuses to "out_file" and show them in console. 
     $ BOOT_BCT -> Boots BCT without applying locks.
     $ PAYLOAD payload.bin [arm|thumb] -> Boots "payload.bin" the entrymode mode can be specified (thumb by default)
+
+## Read the eMMC boot0 BCT prefix
+
+`EMMC_READ_BOOT0_BCT` reads sectors 0–31 from hardware eMMC boot partition 1
+(boot0) over the existing 1-bit ShofEL transport. It does not issue sector
+write or erase commands. The payload temporarily changes only EXT_CSD
+`PARTITION_CONFIG[2:0]` to select boot0, preserves the other bits, and verifies
+that the original byte is restored before it sends any data. The host writes
+exactly 16 KiB to a private temporary file, prints its SHA-256, and installs it
+without replacing an existing output path.
+
+    $ ./shofel2_t124 --usb-port-path 1-1 EMMC_READ_BOOT0_BCT boot0-prefix.bin
+    $ python3 scripts/verify_boot0_bct.py boot0-prefix.bin \
+        --bct-dump /path/to/bct_dump --read-bl-len-exp 9
+
+Pass the `READ_BL_LEN` exponent printed by the reader to check the second
+8 KiB BCT copy's position. NVIDIA's [Tegra Boot Flow redundancy description](https://http.download.nvidia.com/tegra-public-appnotes/tegra-boot-flow.html)
+derives eMMC page size from CSD `READ_BL_LEN` and locates the next copy at
+`PagesPerBct` pages; this verifier requires that copy to begin at byte 8192 so
+both complete early copies fit in the captured prefix.
+The verifier compares all normalized SDRAM[2] fields against the bundled
+Jibo 5.4.2 profile. It rejects any parseable early copy with different
+parameters. `bct_dump` parseability does not verify BootROM signatures, and
+copies in later boot0 journal blocks are outside the captured prefix.
     
 
 ## Interesting facts (maybe some of them wrong)
@@ -60,4 +84,3 @@ Usage
 | void ep1_in_write_imm(void *buffer, u32 size, u32 *num_xfer) | 0x001065C0 | Writes EP1_IN |
 | void ep1_out_read_imm(void *buffer, u32 size, u32 *num_xfer) | 0x00106612 | Reads EP1_OUT |
 | void do_bct_boot() | 0x00100624 | Boots BCT without applying locks. |
